{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789213421,"nonce":"rK/S9mWP4DfZSaVDn3NKGcy9erY=","title":"Typed call bridge, object protocol and error protocol","message":"TypeDesc: hl_type prefix plus caribou tail (lang, protocol vtable, epoch,\nname, adapter ext). One interned symbol table carrying HashLink's field hash.\n\nProtocol messages: get/set member, invoke, call, index/len/iterate,\nto_string/hash/eq, unwrap_native; plus is_error, error_message, error_kind,\nerror_cause, error_trace. Kinds: Runtime, Type, NullAccess, Index,\nArithmetic, User, Cancelled, StackOverflow, OutOfMemory, Internal.\n\nTwo ABIs at the boundary: typed (C function pointer plus hl_type_fun-shaped\nsignature) and dynamic (one 64-bit Value). The bridge, generalised from\nash_native_call and ash_static_call, calls typed from dynamic and wraps\ndynamic callables as typed closures.\n\nEvery boundary is a protected call in both directions: setjmp trap for\nHashLink and HDLLs, fiber-abort boundary for Wren, effect handler for Zyntax,\nstatus for plugins, catch_unwind for Rust. An error leaving a segment becomes\na pending value plus a trace segment and is re-raised natively in the next;\na value returning to its home language is unwrapped; traces stitch.\nResumable effects with a host handler cross as suspend plus continuation.","files":null}]}